<h2 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-PixStoreStorageIntegration">PixStor=
e Storage Integration</h2>
<p>For S3-based storage, AI+ integrates with PixStore which publishes files=
ystem events:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Exchange</strong>: <code>pixstor-fs-events-xchg</code> (fanout)<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Queue</strong>: <code>pixstor-fs-events-xchg_notification-api</c=
ode></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Events</strong>: FileCreated, FileMoved, FileDeleted</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Message format</strong>: Includes S3 object details and optional=
 inode information</p></li>
</ul>
<p>The Notification API consumes these events and routes them to appropriat=
e AI+ services based on configuration.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-QueueManagementStrategy">Queue Mana=
gement Strategy</h2>
<p>Queue management is critical for maintaining system reliability and perf=
ormance. The design employs several strategies to ensure efficient message =
processing and system stability.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-QueueConfigurationandTopology">Queu=
e Configuration and Topology</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Process=
ing Queue Configuration:
  Name: pixstor-fs-events-xchg_notification-api
  Type: Quorum Queue
  Durability: Durable
  Auto-delete: False
  Arguments:
    x-message-ttl: 86400000  # 24 hours
    x-max-length: 10000      # Maximum queue depth
    x-overflow: drop-head    # Drop oldest messages when full
    x-dead-letter-exchange: ai-plus-dlx
    x-delivery-limit: 3      # Max retries before DLX
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-ConsumerManagement">Consumer Manage=
ment</h3>
<p>The system implements intelligent consumer management to handle varying =
workloads:</p>
