=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=98
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-BackpressureandFlowControl">Backpre=
ssure and Flow Control</h3>
<p>To prevent system overload, the design implements backpressure mechanism=
s:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Produce=
r =E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=96=BA RabbitMQ =E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=96=BA Consumer=
 =E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=96=BA Processing Pipeline
    =E2=96=B2            =E2=94=82            =E2=94=82               =E2=
=94=82
    =E2=94=82            =E2=94=82            =E2=94=82               =E2=
=94=82
    =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=B4=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=B4=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=98
         Backpressure Signals:
         - Queue full (x-overflow)
         - Consumer capacity reached
         - Processing pipeline saturated
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Backpressure Strategies:</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Producer Side:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Implement publisher confirms</p></li>
<li>
<p>Retry with exponential backoff when queue is full</p></li>
<li>
<p>Alert when unable to publish for extended periods</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Consumer Side:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Prefetch limit per consumer (e.g., prefetch_count=3D10)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Dynamic consumer scaling based on queue depth</p></li>
<li>
<p>Graceful degradation when overwhelmed</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Processing Pipeline:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Worker pool with maximum capacity</p></li>
<li>
<p>Job queuing with priority support</p></li>
<li>
<p>Resource-based admission control</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-DetailedMessageSpecifications">Deta=
iled Message Specifications</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-PixStoreEventFormat">PixStore Event=
 Format</h3>
<p>For S3 storage events from PixStore, the system receives FileCreated and=
 FileMoved events:</p>
<h4 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-FileCreatedEvent">FileCreated Event=
</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "eventTime": "2025-03-10T15:29:06.667Z",
  "eventName": "FileCreated",
  "tenantId": "iris",
  "source": {
    "fsInode": {
      "fsid": "3156238734335410383",
      "ino": "296962",
      "igen": "1105424809"
    },
    "s3object": {
      "host": "datacore-swarm-ftl.com:8053",
      "bucket": "images",
      "key": "Examples of ingest/image.png",
      "etag": "9ffe930837cca7d70c71bdf5f589a8ae-1",
      "mtime": 1741620429792
    }
  }
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-HTTPRequesttoAI+Services">HTTP Requ=
est to AI+ Services</h3>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"28c83b62-c6a3-441f-a62=
3-0ddfca5b0830">The Notification API transforms PixStore events into HTTP r=
equests for AI+ services with special fields to indicate RabbitMQ result pu=
blishing:</span></p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "job_id": "job-uuid-12345",  // Generated by Notification API
  "media_file": "images/Examples of ingest/image.png",
  "callback_url": null,  // NULL indicates RabbitMQ publishing
  "config": {
    "tenant_id": "iris",
    "source_event": "FileCreated",
    "result_destination": {
      "type": "rabbitmq",
      "exchange": "vision-metadata-xchg",  // Default, configurable
      "routing_key": ""
    },
    "source": {
      // Original source from PixStore event
      "s3object": {
        "host": "datacore-swarm-ftl.com:8053",
        "bucket": "images",
        "key": "Examples of ingest/image.png",
        "etag": "9ffe930837cca7d70c71bdf5f589a8ae-1"
      }
    }
  }
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>When <code>callback_url</code> is null and <code>result_destination.type=
</code> is "rabbitmq", the AI+ service publishes results to RabbitMQ instea=
d of making an HTTP callback.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-StatusUpdateMessages">Status Update=
 Messages</h3>
<p>Status messages provide real-time visibility into job processing:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
  "eventTime": "2025-01-17T10:31:00.000Z",
  "eventName": "JobStatusUpdate",
  "jobId": "job-uuid-12345",
  "tenantId": "tenant-123",
  "correlationId": "corr-uuid-11111",
  "status": "PROCESSING",
  "previousStatus": "WAITING",
  "progress": {
    "percentage": 45,
    "currentStep": "frame_analysis",
    "totalSteps": 5,
    "estimatedTimeRemaining": 180
  },
  "details": {
    "message": "Analyzing video frames for object detection",
    "framesProcessed": 450,
    "totalFrames": 1000,
    "currentFPS": 15.5
  },
  "resources": {
    "cpuUsage": 78.5,
    "memoryUsage": 3.2,
    "gpuUsage": 0
  },
  "source": {
    "s3object": {
      "bucket": "media-files",
      "key": "videos/2025/01/customer-video.mp4"
    }
  }
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-ConfigurationManagement">Configurat=
ion Management</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-ServiceRoutingConfiguration">Servic=
e Routing Configuration</h3>
<p>The Notification API uses Consul configuration to determine how to route=
 PixStore events:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">notific=
ation_api:
  routing:
    # Processing rules by bucket
    buckets:
      media-content:
        # Watch specific folders within bucket
        watch_folders:
          - path: "videos/ingest/"
            recursive: true
            file_patterns:=20
              - "*.mp4"
              - "*.mov"
              - "*.avi"
            exclude_patterns:
              - "*_temp.*"
              - "*_processing.*"
            services:=20
              - metagen
              - object-detection
           =20
          - path: "images/raw/"
            recursive: false
            file_patterns:=20
              - "*.jpg"
              - "*.png"
              - "*.tiff"
            services:=20
              - metagen
              - facial-recognition
     =20
      documents:
        # Process entire bucket
        watch_folders:
          - path: "/"
            recursive: true
            file_patterns:=20
              - "*.pdf"
              - "*.docx"
            services:=20
              - summarization
   =20
    # Service endpoints
    services:
      metagen:
        endpoint: "http://ai-plus-metagen.service.consul:8080/process"
        enabled: true
        max_file_size: "10GB"
        timeout: 3600
       =20
      facial-recognition:
        endpoint: "http://ai-plus-facial.service.consul:8080/process"
        enabled: false
        max_file_size: "50MB"
        timeout: 300
   =20
    # Result destination defaults
    result_destinations:
      default:
        type: "rabbitmq"
        exchange: "vision-metadata-xchg"
     =20
      # Service-specific overrides
      summarization:
        type: "rabbitmq"
        exchange: "document-metadata-xchg"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-RabbitMQConfiguration">RabbitMQ Con=
figuration</h3>
<p>The RabbitMQ integration extends the existing BaseConfig system:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">{
    "service": {
        "component_name": "notification-api",
        "host": "0.0.0.0",
        "port": 8080
    },
    "rabbitmq": {
        "enabled": true,
        "connection": {
            "host": "rabbitmq.service.consul",
            "port": 5672,
            "vhost": "/",
            "username": "{vault.rabbitmq.username}",
            "password": "{vault.rabbitmq.password}",
            "connection_attempts": 3,
            "retry_delay": 2,
            "heartbeat": 600,
            "blocked_connection_timeout": 300
        },
        "tls": {
            "enabled": true,
            "verify_mode": "CERT_REQUIRED",
            "ca_path": "/etc/aiplus/certs/ca.pem"
        },
        "consumer": {
            "prefetch_count": 10,
            "auto_ack": false,
            "exclusive": false,
            "consumer_tag": "notification-api"
        },
        "exchanges": {
            "pixstore": {
                "name": "pixstor-fs-events-xchg",
                "type": "fanout",
                "durable": true
            },
            "status": {
                "name": "ai-plus-status-xchg",
                "type": "topic",
                "durable": true
            },
            "result": {
                "name": "vision-metadata-xchg",
                "type": "fanout",
                "durable": true
            }
        },
        "queues": {
            "processing": {
                "name": "pixstor-fs-events-xchg_notification-api",
                "durable": true,
                "exclusive": false,
                "auto_delete": false,
                "arguments": {
                    "x-message-ttl": 86400000,
                    "x-max-length": 10000,
                    "x-overflow": "drop-head",
                    "x-dead-letter-exchange": "ai-plus-dlx",
                    "x-delivery-limit": 3
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-S3EventProcessing">S3 Event Process=
ing</h2>
<p>This section details the specific implementation for processing S3 stora=
ge events from PixStore.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-S3ProcessingStateManagement">S3 Pro=
cessing State Management</h3>
<p>AI+ services use S3 object metadata to track processing state per servic=
e:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># S3 Me=
tadata Schema
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-{service}-status: "processed|failed"
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-{service}-time: "2025-01-17T10:00:00Z"
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-{service}-version: "1.0.0"
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-{service}-error: "error message if failed"

# Example for metagen service
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-status: "processed"
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-time: "2025-01-17T10:00:00Z"
x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-version: "1.0.0"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-SequenceDiagrams">Sequence Diagrams=
</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-FileCreatedEventProcessing"><span c=
lass=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"bafb78f8-9eea-4aa3-9d65-50bde544=
f21d">FileCreated Event Processing</span></h4>
<p>This sequence shows the complete flow from file upload to metadata index=
ing in Vision.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sequenc=
eDiagram
    participant User
    participant S3 as S3 Storage
    participant PS as PixStore
    participant RMQ as RabbitMQ
    participant NA as Notification API
    participant AI as AI+ Service
    participant Vision

    Note over User,Vision: Happy Path - New File Processing
   =20
    User-&gt;&gt;S3: PUT object (video.mp4)
    S3-&gt;&gt;PS: Object created notification
    PS-&gt;&gt;PS: Detect new file
   =20
    PS-&gt;&gt;RMQ: Publish FileCreated event
    Note right of PS: Exchange: pixstor-fs-events-xchg&lt;br/&gt;Event incl=
udes S3 location,&lt;br/&gt;tenant ID, etag, mtime
   =20
    RMQ-&gt;&gt;NA: Deliver FileCreated message
    Note right of RMQ: Queue: pixstor-fs-events-xchg_notification-api
   =20
    NA-&gt;&gt;NA: Validate message format
    NA-&gt;&gt;NA: Check routing configuration
    Note right of NA: - Is bucket monitored?&lt;br/&gt;- Does path match wa=
tch folder?&lt;br/&gt;- Which services should process?
   =20
    alt File should be processed
        NA-&gt;&gt;NA: Generate job ID
        NA-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK message
       =20
        NA-&gt;&gt;AI: POST /process
        Note right of NA: job_id: generated&lt;br/&gt;callback_url: null&lt=
;br/&gt;result_destination: rabbitmq
       =20
        AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Detect RabbitMQ mode
        Note right of AI: callback_url is null,&lt;br/&gt;use RabbitMQ for =
results
       =20
        AI-&gt;&gt;S3: HEAD object (check metadata)
        S3--&gt;&gt;AI: Object metadata
       =20
        AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Check if already processed
        Note right of AI: Look for x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-status
       =20
        alt Not yet processed
            AI-&gt;&gt;S3: GET object (download file)
            S3--&gt;&gt;AI: File content
           =20
            AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Process with MetaGen
            Note right of AI: Generate metadata:&lt;br/&gt;- Summary&lt;br/=
&gt;- Keywords&lt;br/&gt;- Scene analysis
           =20
            AI-&gt;&gt;S3: Update object metadata
            Note right of AI: Set x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-status =3D "pr=
ocessed"
           =20
            AI-&gt;&gt;RMQ: Publish MetadataGenerated event
            Note right of AI: Exchange: vision-metadata-xchg&lt;br/&gt;Incl=
ude source S3 location&lt;br/&gt;and generated metadata
           =20
            RMQ-&gt;&gt;Vision: Deliver metadata
            Vision-&gt;&gt;Vision: Index metadata
            Vision-&gt;&gt;Vision: Associate with source file
            Vision-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK message
           =20
        else Already processed
            AI-&gt;&gt;NA: 200 OK (already processed)
        end
       =20
    else File should not be processed
        NA-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK message (skip)
        Note right of NA: File doesn't match routing rules
    end
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-ExtendedUseCase1:FileMovedDuringPro=
cessing"><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e5809029-6955-48=
4b-b321-67315d7a3780">Extended Use Case 1</span>: FileMoved During Processi=
ng</h4>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"ecb1d0a1-9f8e-47d7-b21=
5-5e90c19b377b">This</span> sequence shows how AI+ handles file movements t=
hat occur while processing is in progress.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sequenc=
eDiagram
    participant User
    participant S3
    participant PS as PixStore
    participant RMQ as RabbitMQ
    participant NA as Notification API
    participant AI as AI+ Service
    participant Vision

    Note over AI: Currently processing video.mp4 (50% complete)
   =20
    User-&gt;&gt;S3: Copy object to archive/video.mp4
    User-&gt;&gt;S3: Delete original video.mp4
   =20
    S3-&gt;&gt;PS: Object deleted + created notifications
    PS-&gt;&gt;PS: Correlate as move operation
   =20
    PS-&gt;&gt;RMQ: Publish FileMoved event
    Note right of PS: source: bucket/video.mp4&lt;br/&gt;target: bucket/arc=
hive/video.mp4
   =20
    RMQ-&gt;&gt;NA: Deliver FileMoved message
   =20
    NA-&gt;&gt;NA: Check if job exists for source
    Note right of NA: Track active jobs by S3 location
   =20
    alt Job exists for source file
        NA-&gt;&gt;AI: POST /update-location
        Note right of NA: Notify AI+ of new location
       =20
        AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Check active jobs
        AI-&gt;&gt;S3: HEAD source object
       =20
        alt Source still accessible (race condition)
            S3--&gt;&gt;AI: Object exists
            AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Continue processing
            AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Update job target location
            Note right of AI: Will publish result with&lt;br/&gt;new locati=
on
            AI-&gt;&gt;NA: 200 OK
           =20
            AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Complete processing
            AI-&gt;&gt;S3: Update metadata at NEW location
            Note right of AI: Set processed flag on archive/video.mp4
           =20
            AI-&gt;&gt;RMQ: Publish MetadataGenerated
            Note right of AI: source points to NEW location
           =20
        else Source no longer accessible
            S3--&gt;&gt;AI: 404 Not Found
            AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Cancel active job
            AI-&gt;&gt;NA: 200 OK (job cancelled)
           =20
            Note right of NA: Wait for new FileCreated&lt;br/&gt;at target =
location
        end
       =20
    else No active job for file
        NA-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK FileMoved (ignore)
        Note right of NA: Not currently processing this file
    end
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h4 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-ExtendedUseCase2:DuplicateProcessin=
gPrevention">Extended Use Case 2: Duplicate Processing Prevention</h4>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e29a51f2-aef4-48b6-933=
e-a4d420180aa5">This sequence demonstrates</span> how the system prevents d=
uplicate processing when multiple events arrive.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sequenc=
eDiagram
    participant PS as PixStore
    participant RMQ as RabbitMQ
    participant NA1 as Notification API 1
    participant NA2 as Notification API 2
    participant AI as AI+ Service
    participant S3

    PS-&gt;&gt;RMQ: Publish FileCreated
   =20
    Note over RMQ: Multiple consumers for HA
   =20
    par Concurrent Delivery
        RMQ-&gt;&gt;NA1: FileCreated (video.mp4)
    and
        RMQ-&gt;&gt;NA2: FileCreated (video.mp4)
    end
   =20
    NA1-&gt;&gt;NA1: Generate job-id-1
    NA2-&gt;&gt;NA2: Generate job-id-2
   =20
    NA1-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK message
    NA2-&gt;&gt;RMQ: ACK message
   =20
    par Both send to AI+
        NA1-&gt;&gt;AI: POST /process (job-id-1)
    and
        NA2-&gt;&gt;AI: POST /process (job-id-2)
    end
   =20
    AI-&gt;&gt;S3: HEAD object (check metadata)
    S3--&gt;&gt;AI: No processed flag
   =20
    AI-&gt;&gt;AI: Accept job-id-1
    AI-&gt;&gt;NA1: 202 Accepted
   =20
    AI-&gt;&gt;S3: Set processing flag (atomic)
    Note right of AI: x-amz-meta-ai-plus-metagen-processing =3D "true"
   =20
    AI-&gt;&gt;S3: HEAD object (for job-id-2)
    S3--&gt;&gt;AI: Processing flag exists
   =20
    AI-&gt;&gt;NA2: 409 Conflict (already processing)
    Note right of AI: Another job is processing this file
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-MessageProcessingLogic">Message Pro=
cessing Logic</h3>
<h4 id=3D"AI-284:AI+RabbitMQIntegration-FileCreatedEventHandler(Notificatio=
nAPI)">FileCreated Event Handler (Notification API)</h4>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
